    "updated_at": "2025-08-29T11:52:23Z",
    "body": "Yeah, I'm in favour of making the default behaviour more accessible, i.e. having the baseline be *not* to play *unless* the author has taken the extra step of adding `\"despite-prefers-reduced-motion\"`.\n\nI don't really know how to assess web compatibility here: some videos would stop autoplaying, yes, but I think there is a reasonable argument to be made that that behaviour was always potentially user-hostile. Autoplaying can even be outright dangerous in extreme cases, such as when people have epilepsy.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
