    "updated_at": "2025-08-29T11:58:27Z",
    "body": "I worry about cases like this:\n\nThe developer has created a complex animation that involves CSS animations, JS animations, and video. They care about accessibility, so if the user prefers-reduced-motion, the developer shows a custom play button, instead of starting the animation automatically.\n\nOnce play is pressed, they start their CSS & JS animations, and insert `<video autoplay>` to handle the video stuff.\n\nWith https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9900 we'd break parts of their animation.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
