    "created_at": "2025-08-29T12:53:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-29T12:53:25Z",
    "body": "> It would create an asymmetry with things like CSS animations, and animated image formats. It seems like the model of the platform is not to handle prefers-reduced-motion automatically. We had a similar discussion with view transitions.\n\nLike I mentioned elsewhere I think there's a strong discussion to be had to change this default across the board, in the most web compatible way possible. Naive outdated styles that I've used before. Not impossible to undo but something you have to think about. Wouldn't work as UA styles but I think we could consider something of that sort.\n\n```css\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n    *, ::before, ::after {\n        animation-delay: -1ms !important;\n        animation-duration: 1ms !important;\n        animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;\n        background-attachment: initial !important;\n        scroll-behavior: auto !important;\n        transition-duration: 0s !important;\n        transition-delay: 0s !important;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nEither way not to distract from the main point of this issue I think some way to honour it would be good even if opt-in.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
