    "updated_at": "2025-08-29T13:15:56Z",
    "body": "> We had a similar discussion with view transitions.\n\nCould you point us to that conversation? The fact that these effects (currently) play despite `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` still baffles me.\n\n> This is somewhat reasonable, as it isn't \"prefer no motion\" […]\n\nThe fact that (on Windows) users communicate this preference by turning off the system toggle labelled ***Animation Effects*** (not _\"motion effects\"_) seem like a good counterargument, since arguably playing video _is_ an animation, and could be considered _effect_.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
